3. CONTRIBUTIONS AND ASSIGNMENT REQUIREMENT

Bug reports and proposed fixes are welcome under the repository's
CONTRIBUTING.md rules. Submitting a pull request does not guarantee acceptance
or merging. Every proposed change must be reviewed and explicitly approved by
the project maintainer before it can be incorporated.

A contribution is NOT transferred to Likounsee merely because it is submitted,
reviewed, discussed, or mentioned in a pull request. Before any third-party
code or other copyrightable contribution is merged, distributed, or otherwise
incorporated into Amethys Launcher, its contributor must sign a separate
written contribution and intellectual-property assignment agreement covering
that specific contribution. The agreement must identify the contribution and
clearly specify the rights assigned and the permitted scope of exploitation,
in accordance with applicable law.

Subject to that signed agreement and applicable law, the contributor assigns
to Likounsee the agreed transferable economic rights in the accepted
contribution, including the expressly identified rights to reproduce, modify,
adapt, translate, integrate, distribute, make available, and commercially or
otherwise exploit it as part of Amethys Launcher and its related releases,
in source-code and object-code form. The assignment's territory, duration,
purposes, and any compensation must be stated in the individual agreement.
No assignment of all of a person's future works is intended.

The contributor will be credited in CONTRIBUTORS.md where reasonably
practicable and as specified in the contribution process. Credit does not
give the contributor ownership or control over the Project Materials or the
assigned economic rights. Nothing here purports to transfer or waive moral
rights that cannot legally be transferred or waived. In particular, mandatory
rights under applicable law remain unaffected.

Security-sensitive contributions are subject to the same prior written
assignment requirement and must additionally pass the project's security and
confidentiality review. Access to, possession of, or authorship of security
code does not by itself create any special ownership transfer. Any assignment
must be made through the same specific written agreement described above.
Security reports and confidential information must follow SECURITY.md and
must not be disclosed in public issues or pull requests.

A contributor must not submit code or materials they do not have the right to
contribute, or that violate another party's rights, confidentiality
obligations, contractual restrictions, or applicable law. Until the required
written agreement is signed and the contribution is accepted, the contributor
retains their rights and Likounsee has no right to incorporate or exploit the
contribution beyond what is strictly necessary to review it.

